# KIT Iteration — REQ-011

## Targeted REQ

REQ-011 — Task inbox and state badges

## In Scope

- Task inbox page listing open workflow tasks
- State badge component for all five workflow states
- Task row with document detail navigation via Next.js Link (client-side routing)
- Retry action conditionally shown for exception tasks with permission, with loading/disabled state
- Auto-refresh via TanStack Query (polling) without full page reload
- Read state tracking via dedicated `useReadState` hook with localStorage persistence
- Italian labels for all operator-visible text
- Component tests proving all five acceptance criteria
- Auth context seam in page.tsx ready for promotion-time swap

## Out of Scope

- Backend task API implementation (REQ-010)
- Document detail page (REQ-007)
- Playwright E2E tests (deferred to integration phase)
- Shared UI component library creation (assumed from REQ-004)
- WebSocket real-time updates (polling is sufficient for pilot)

## Implementation Summary

The inbox is built as a Next.js page at the `workflow/inbox` route. It uses TanStack Query for server state with 30-second polling for background refresh. The task list is fetched from `GET /api/tasks?status=open,in_progress` and rendered as a table with:

- **StateBadge** — color-coded badge mapping each of the five backend enum values to Italian labels and Tailwind color classes. Includes graceful fallback for unknown values.
- **TaskRow** — displays document_id, task type, status badge, creation time, assignment, and conditionally renders a retry button for exception tasks when the user has the `validate` permission. Uses Next.js `Link` for client-side navigation to `/documents/{document_id}`. Retry button shows loading state while mutation is pending.
- **TaskInbox** — orchestrates the list, handles empty state, loading, and error states in Italian. Exposes a hidden `data-updated-at` timestamp for test assertions on data freshness.

Navigation to document detail uses Next.js `Link` component for client-side routing without full page reload.

Read state is tracked via a dedicated `useReadState` hook that persists read task IDs to localStorage, avoiding full page reload for visual updates.

The page component (`page.tsx`) contains an explicit auth context seam (`useAuthUser`) documented for replacement at promotion time with the shared auth hook from REQ-002/REQ-004.

## Hooks

| Hook | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `useTasks` | TanStack Query hook with 30s polling interval. Exports `TASK_QUERY_KEY` and `POLL_INTERVAL_MS` constants. |
| `useRetryTask` | Mutation hook that calls `POST /api/documents/{id}/retry` and invalidates the task query cache on success. |
| `useReadState` | Manages read/unread state via localStorage. Returns `readIds`, `markRead`, and `isRead`. |

## Tests Added or Updated

| Test file | What it proves |
|---|---|
| `TaskInbox.test.tsx` | Lists tasks with correct columns; empty state; loading state; error state; retry button visibility based on task type and permission; retry triggers API call and cache invalidation (verified via fetch counter); row click marks as read with localStorage persistence; read state restored from localStorage on mount; data-updated-at timestamp proves SPA-style data fetch; cache invalidation after retry triggers refetch without page reload |
| `StateBadge.test.tsx` | All five workflow states render correct Italian label and color class; unknown status fallback |

## Test Infrastructure

- Tests mock `next/link` as a plain `<a>` tag for jsdom compatibility.
- MSW setup includes a fetch counter (`getFetchCount`/`resetFetchCount`) to assert cache invalidation behavior.
- TaskInbox exposes a hidden `data-updated-at` element for test assertions on TanStack Query data freshness.

## Execution Notes

- Tests use MSW 2.x to intercept API calls, providing deterministic task fixtures.
- No real backend or network required.
- `jsdom` environment for Vitest.
- Coverage target: 75% (frontend lane).

## Assumptions

- Backend task list API returns `{ tasks: TaskDTO[] }` with fields: `id`, `document_id`, `task_type`, `status`, `document_status`, `assigned_to`, `created_at`, `completed_at`, `source_filename`.
- Auth context provides `user.permissions: string[]` including `"validate"` for retry eligibility.
- Shared API client from `frontend.app.shared.api` provides `apiClient` with base URL and auth headers. Fallback provided inline for standalone testing.
- Italian localization is hardcoded for slice-1; i18n framework is not introduced.

