# HOWTO — REQ-011

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 20.x
- npm 10.x
- No backend or AWS services required for tests (MSW mocks all API calls)

## Runtime Profiles

### Local (development & testing)
- All API calls intercepted by MSW
- No network dependencies
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000` (used by MSW handlers)

### AWS (target deployment)
- Next.js build deployed to ECS Fargate
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` points to internal FastAPI ALB
- Auth via OIDC/SAML IdP token in `Authorization` header

## Environment Setup

bash
export NODE_ENV=test
export NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000

## Install

bash
cd runs/kit/REQ-011
npm ci

If a `package.json` is not yet present at the staging root, copy or link from the canonical frontend workspace. The emitted source files are designed for promotion into the canonical `src/` tree.

## Local Run Commands

bash
# Run all component tests
npx vitest run --reporter=verbose

# Run with coverage
npx vitest run --coverage

# Run specific test suite
npx vitest run --testPathPattern=TaskInbox
npx vitest run --testPathPattern=StateBadge

# Lint
