## Test Infrastructure Notes

### Next.js Link mock
Tests mock `next/link` as a plain `<a>` tag via `vi.mock("next/link", ...)` since jsdom does not provide the full Next.js router. The mock preserves `href` and all other props so navigation assertions work correctly.

### MSW fetch counter
The test setup exports `getFetchCount()` and `resetFetchCount()` to assert that TanStack Query cache invalidation triggers actual refetches. This is used in AC-4 (retry triggers refetch) and AC-5 (refresh without reload) tests.

### data-updated-at element
`TaskInbox` renders a hidden `<span data-testid="data-updated-at">` containing the TanStack Query `dataUpdatedAt` timestamp. Tests use this to prove data was fetched via the query hook (SPA-style) rather than a full page load.

## Troubleshooting

### `Cannot find module` errors
Ensure `npm ci` has been run. If testing in isolation, verify that `vitest.config.ts` path aliases match the emitted structure.

### MSW handler not intercepting
Check that `setup.ts` is imported in the test file's `beforeAll`. MSW 2.x requires explicit `server.listen()`.

### TanStack Query warnings
Wrap test renders in `QueryClientProvider` with a fresh `QueryClient` per test. The test setup file handles this.

### TypeScript errors on shared imports
The emitted code references `frontend.app.shared.*` modules from prior REQs. For standalone testing, inline fallbacks are provided. For full integration, ensure REQ-004 shared modules are available.

### Next.js Link errors in tests
The `vi.mock("next/link", ...)` in `TaskInbox.test.tsx` replaces the real Link component. If you see "Cannot find module next/link", ensure `next` is installed as a dev dependency.
